WEBVTT

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:35.910
Love Means Never Feeling Regret

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.520
Arima. It's too soon.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.820
Really?

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.820
I don't think one or two minutes 
makes a difference, myself...

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.200
Those who are negligent in etiquette 
will be negligent in all things.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.830
Lifestyle, academics,

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.340
self-respect...

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.460
Yes, yes. Whatever you say.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.240
President Kusatsu is as strict as ever.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:01.490
Akoya, it is easy to drift downwards.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.350
We, the student council of Binan High School,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.180
regard foolishness and mediocrity as a sin.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:07.690
We must not approve of it.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.360
Understood.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:13.110
Here you are. This is Seishodo's "White Dew."

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.030
Arima-san, it's delicious.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.800
Glad to hear it.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.560
It was worth sending away for.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.470
Now, rulers of this blue world.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.980
Members of the noble Caerula Adamas.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:35.260
Let us begin the executive meeting of the 
Total Conquest of Earth's Lifeforms Project.

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:37.070
<i>Feel the power...</i>

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.370
<i>Of love!</i>

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:45.180
Why are their faces blurred out? 
Their voices are strange, too.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:47.650
We haven't done anything to it.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.650
It seems they scrambled the 
information themselves.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.100
<i>Love is over!</i>

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:59.110
Do you think they intend to interrupt our
Total Conquest of Earth's Lifeforms Project,

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:00.960
Lord Zundar?

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.080
The possibility exists.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:07.540
Does that mean they've been given 
the same technology we have?

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:14.760
That voice and image filter is a product 
of highly advanced scientific technology.

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.010
You mean that "voices have been changed 
in the interests of privacy" thing?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:23.280
It is on par with the scientific 
technology of my planet.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.060
Planet Evil, you mean?

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:27.110
Correct.

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:31.110
If they do exist to oppose us, 
we will need to take caution.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:34.580
The things they wear and say 
have no style whatsoever.

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.270
They can't possibly compete with us.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.020
Or should I say, I dislike even the 
idea of thinking them as equals.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.370
I suppose we should watch them for a while?

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.570
If they appear next time, we will 
need to consider countermeasures.

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:50.060
For now, let us move forward 
with the Earth Conquest Project.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:54.500
Yes. The superior should rule and 
guide the world's development.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:59.040
To this end, the foolish and the acts 
of barbarism they commit must be purged.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.100
That's quite the ambitious undertaking, I must say.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:04.020
Well then, Arima...

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.480
The state of this Earth.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:06.930
This city.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.900
This school. Do you approve of it?

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.860
Base and vulgar.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:13.810
Ignorant and incompetent.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.240
Stupid and silly.

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:19.020
Should such students run
rampant over Binan High School?

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.780
Oh, well...

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:26.240
I do think some degree of 
order might be necessary.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:31.040
Which means we must first establish a 
model society in our immediate vicinity.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:31.830
Namely...

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.500
The Binan High School Conquest Project, right?

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.530
I unilaterally agree with President Kusatsu.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.930
I don't want to look at ugly and dirty things.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:47.810
The inferior beings should fight with 
their fellows, and destroy themselves.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.130
That's entirely logical.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:54.520
Then you should make use of the humans' 
short-tempered, violent natures.

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:57.650
First, we need someone who 
can execute the operation.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:05:02.320
Find someone to be our puppet, 
and act through them, right?

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.550
Correct.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.810
Lend him just a bit of our power.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.580
Anger, hatred, jealousy...

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:14.080
They burn more easily than dry leaves.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.820
Understood, Lord Zundar.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:19.000
Then let us find us our fool at once.

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:21.970
Caerula Adamas, I leave this to you.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.050
Sir!

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:26.690
Did you know?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.300
People say it's not true 
that forests are disappearing

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.050
to make disposable chopsticks.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.020
Where did that come from, Yufuin-senpai?

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.110
Disposable chopsticks are made from 
trees cut down to thin out forests,

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:41.190
so they're logical from an eco-friendly, 
recycling point of view.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:43.280
I know that.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:46.620
Well then, the phrase "boiled down"

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:49.710
originally referred to reaching a 
conclusion after a lengthy discussion.

00:05:50.300 --> 00:05:51.290
Did you know that?

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:53.750
A crime of conscience or 
inappropriate laughter, right?

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.500
Speaking of disposable 
chopsticks getting boiled down,

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.830
my bro Gora taught me...

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.540
"Menma is just recycled disposable chopsticks."

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:01.510
Wow, he's an idiot.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:04.010
But it's kinda like disposable chopsticks, isn't it?

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.830
It's just thin and rectangular, right?

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:07.320
It's also crisp.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.560
That doesn't mean it's chopsticks.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:11.490
The crispiness comes from the 
bamboo it's made from.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:13.440
There are disposable chopsticks 
made from bamboo, too.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:16.060
Are you that determined to 
say menma is chopsticks?

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.420
What are you saying, Ryuu-senpai?

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.770
Menma is menma.

00:06:19.770 --> 00:06:21.720
You're the one who brought it up!

00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:26.030
Anyway, can we talk about why 
Wombat appears to be dead now?

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:28.380
I need one cuddle a day!

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.860
I have no idea why that deserves a thumbs up.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.390
What? It's the obvious compensation.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:35.710
For what?

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:39.270
You know, for the fight... 
The Love Busters thing.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:41.530
Oh. Yeah.

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:45.880
It's not the Love Busters! 
It's the Battle Lovers!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:49.250
At least try to remember your own name!

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.370
Love Battlers, Bust Lovers...

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:54.760
They're both embarrassing, 
so what's the difference?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.080
Battle Lovers is a venerable and noble title!

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.000
Can't be, it's English.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.710
At least be consistent about whether 
you're an alien or a foreigner.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:03.250
So inconsistent.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.150
Plus...

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:08.480
These things won't come off.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:12.000
They're not "these things"! 
They're Lovracelets!

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.290
Yeah.

00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:17.580
The inability to remember proper names 
means you're getting old, you know.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:20.080
Seriously? Is it bad?

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.690
It's bad, Yufuin-senpai.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.920
Trying to have a conversation on nothing but 
"these things," "those things," and "that thing"

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.300
definitely means you're getting old.

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.450
So, there's one person here
who hasn't said a single word,

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.020
let alone a proper name.

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.020
Mr. Tawarayama there.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.440
No! He'll rot!

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:42.690
Now you need not worry.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.500
No, no, no...

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:46.140
"Need not" in this day and age...

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.620
What did you mean, "rot"?

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:51.170
What I mean is, if I get too far away,

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.660
this body's cellular metabolism will cease and...

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.120
You mean he's dead?

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.240
In your planet's terms.

00:07:59.310 --> 00:08:00.160
That's a corpse?

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.690
Dead? So you killed him?

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:02.690
Murderer!

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:03.800
That's a crime.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.500
Cold?

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.640
I don't know how you can touch him, Yumoto.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.640
Yeah? But he's not that cold!

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:11.840
But he's dead!

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:11.840
Liar!

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.120
Wait a minute.

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:15.510
This individual is dead, but he is also alive.

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:19.730
What's with the Schrödinger reference?

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:21.690
No, it's true!

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.140
This is starting to annoy me.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:29.820
I shall describe my current ability to 
function independently as "difficult."

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:33.540
That old man speak is really irritating me.

00:08:33.540 --> 00:08:35.520
You've got our teacher's character all wrong.

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:37.500
He seriously seems possessed.

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:42.000
I am currently in stasis, 
but I shall recover shortly.

00:08:42.350 --> 00:08:43.410
Even though you're dead?

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:47.960
Scientifically advanced medical mechanisms 
are currently at work in my body.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.170
You need not worry.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.090
Easier said than done.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:55.330
As long as I am within a certain range, 
his life will not be in danger.

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:56.820
You know the saying.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.110
We are "living jointly"!

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.620
I don't know where you pulled that one from...

00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:04.300
Putting off dealing with problems 
is called the Concorde Effect.

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:06.010
It just increases your debt.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:09.530
Besides, you can't say you love Earth
when you killed someone on it.

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:11.780
There was a reason for that!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:12.660
What's the reason?

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:16.850
It happened the other day, 
just after I arrived on Earth!

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:19.460
When I was expressing my admiration

00:09:19.460 --> 00:09:23.430
for the generous character and 
clean habits of the people of Earth!

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.790
Does he mean the public bath?

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.080
It's us!

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:28.020
The Kurotama Bath is always open for business!

00:09:28.020 --> 00:09:32.810
But then I was chased around by 
an extremely belligerent individual!

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.010
Huh? Who was that?

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:35.960
Me?!

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:37.470
Ah.

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.220
In order to escape his relentless pursuit,

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.450
I had no choice but to run with all my might!

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:45.480
Help me!

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:07.540
You did it, huh?

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.560
You sure did it.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:09.770
You did it, all right.

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.400
Really did it.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:13.830
Y-Yes, but...

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:17.430
Is the responsibility truly mine alone to bear?

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:18.850
What? Me?

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:22.260
Well, given the force he was 
about to get cuddled with,

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:24.230
maybe he was right to run.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.880
"Sekuhara"? No, you'd call it "anihara," right?

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:28.660
Animal harassment, yeah.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.070
I get it.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:33.780
In that case, Wombat, cuddle me!

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:35.210
As much as you like.

00:10:35.210 --> 00:10:37.420
Do it to your heart's content!

00:10:37.420 --> 00:10:38.860
I refuse!

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:39.490
Why?!

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:43.760
I don't want cuddles, I want you 
to work as the Battle Lovers!

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:46.510
What I want more than anything 
is for you to love the Earth!

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:48.800
But you can just love me!

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:50.840
Question.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.940
You mean we'll have to put on 
those weird costumes again?

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:57.830
More than the costumes, I disliked 
those grandiose introductory speeches.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:59.430
If it were just the costume...

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:02.710
What? "If"? You mean you'd be fine
if it was just the costume?

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:05.440
If I think of it as cosplay, it's totally fine.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:06.830
We can fire beams, too!

00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:07.900
Now that you mention it...

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:12.850
Well, if my cute li'l Wombat 
asks it of me, I'll take it on!

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.190
Hold on a minute.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.320
Can you really take something 
like this on that easily?

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.070
And how long will we have to do it?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:23.110
Until the Earth is filled with love, naturally!

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:24.850
You're so creepy.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:27.330
Love? What's that?

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.840
It's like, being happy, right?

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:31.210
Like me. Or me.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:33.050
Just you, huh, Ryuu?

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:36.870
I think love is found in the 
trivial, realistic moments.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:39.250
Like sharing a can of coffee with a girl,

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:41.900
or when your shoulders brush 
when the train shakes!

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:46.210
I bet I'll feel love when I get 
one billion in my Cayman Islands account.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:47.270
<b>One Billion</b>

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:47.270
Talk about corrupt!

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:50.180
It's fine that everyone has 
his own definition of love.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:53.320
But are you okay with having
 to wear embarrassing costumes,

00:11:53.320 --> 00:11:55.620
say embarrassing lines, 
and do embarrassing things

00:11:55.620 --> 00:11:57.280
for the foreseeable future?

00:11:57.280 --> 00:12:00.350
I told you, it's nothing 
to be embarrassed about!

00:12:00.350 --> 00:12:01.960
By the way...

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.030
Is it okay for you to be away 
from Mr. Tawarayama right now?

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:08.310
It is fine.

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:12.280
Freezing and thawing something over 
and over makes it brittle, y'know?

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:14.390
You need to take care with perishables.

00:12:14.390 --> 00:12:15.480
Like sell-by dates.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.280
I'm sorry!

00:12:17.280 --> 00:12:19.520
It's okay. I don't mind it so much.

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:20.880
You <i>should</i> mind!

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:25.940
<b>Yufuin En
Born July 2nd
Blood Type B / Cancer
Hobby: Napping
Likes: Sleeping in, hot spring manju</b>

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:28.420
<b>On sale this week                                                   New menu item!</b>

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:28.420
<b>Chicken Cutlet Curry                                                           Tanmen</b>

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.050
Now then...

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:36.020
That stench...

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.270
What's wrong?

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:39.880
Kinshiro hates curry to death.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.970
<b>Hashida Wario</b>

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:46.970
<i>My name is Hashida Wario.</i>

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:51.050
<i>I like a world of order and rules.</i>

00:12:51.510 --> 00:12:53.540
<i>The thing I hate most is pi.</i>

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.040
<i>Because it doesn't divide evenly.</i>

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.520
<i>On that note, I also hate 
families with three children.</i>

00:12:57.520 --> 00:13:00.720
<i>When parents and grandparents get 
together for birthdays and Christmas</i>

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.390
<i>and you have seven people sharing a cake...</i>

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:05.850
<i>It's unbearable.</i>

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:09.010
<i>It would be better if the 
grandparents would just...</i>

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:14.360
He is the one.

00:13:14.900 --> 00:13:15.900
Why?

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:20.320
His narrow-minded heart that permits 
no compromise will create a raging flame.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.530
Yes, Lord Zundar.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:28.120
Conquest!

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:35.500
The Golden Chevalier, shining in radiance!

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.850
Aurite!

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.510
The Silver Chevalier, rustling young leaves!

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:43.910
Argent!

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.540
The Pearl Chevalier, making flowers bloom!

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.140
Perlite!

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:55.030
We are the rulers of this blue world...

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:56.980
Caerula Adamas!

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:01.040
Now, release the Zundar Needle!

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:03.910
Aurum!

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:05.590
Argentum!

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:06.970
Perla!

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:11.950
Donum!

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:34.980
That which is not evenly divisible!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:37.170
That which is warped!
That which is not equal!

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.920
Multiply further!

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:42.650
Warp this world and destroy it!

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.740
Asymmetry Beam, fire!

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:54.570
Hey!

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:55.740
Move your hand!

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.060
I can't get to the chopsticks!

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.210
That's <i>your</i> fault!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:08.480
Are mismatched chopsticks really 
enough to start a fight like this?

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:10.390
It really is fighting and self-destruction.

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:13.850
Their own foolishness is to blame.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.920
The Lovracelet's reacting,

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:19.910
but there's no need for all of us to go, right?

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:21.110
I'm taking today off.

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:23.710
You mean it, Yufuin-senpai?

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:26.930
Roger that. If we're short on 
people, we might call you, though.

00:15:26.930 --> 00:15:28.480
Okay, permission given.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:31.260
Hey! Wait just one minute!

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:35.000
Since ancient times, there have always 
been five heirs to the throne of love!

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.440
What, really?

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:41.420
I can't allow you to reduce and 
revert their numbers so lightly!

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.010
What? Sounds like a pain.

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:45.550
Why do you think I went to all that trouble

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.120
of thinking up five introductory speeches?!

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:50.360
What, you thought up those lines?

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:53.220
No wonder I thought they had no style.

00:15:53.800 --> 00:15:56.290
But I spent a whole week thinking them up...

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:57.470
They have no style.

00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:59.140
You said it twice!

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:02.920
Well, I think it's best if all five of us go.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:04.610
See? See? See?!

00:16:04.610 --> 00:16:05.360
How come?

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:06.940
Just a feeling, I guess.

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:10.700
Or maybe I just like odd numbers
 better than even ones!

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:14.200
That's a more unintelligible 
reason than I was expecting.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.080
And we already went out together once!

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.380
It's true that it feels more complete that way.

00:16:18.380 --> 00:16:20.730
And you like that outfit, right, Ryuu?

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:23.970
It really does look good on me...

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:27.070
I don't care! Just, please, get out there!

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:28.260
Guess I don't have a choice.

00:16:29.480 --> 00:16:30.430
Might as well go.

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:34.870
Then Love Making into the 
Battle Lovers right now!

00:16:37.530 --> 00:16:38.830
Love Making!

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:43.120
The Sparkling Prince!

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:44.940
Battle Lover Scarlet!

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:46.770
The Flashing Prince!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.690
Battle Lover Cerulean!

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:50.260
The Piercing Prince!

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:52.270
Battle Lover Epinard!

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:53.860
The Roaring Prince!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.950
Battle Lover Sulfur!

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:57.890
The Thrilling Prince!

00:16:57.890 --> 00:16:59.790
Battle Lover Vesta!

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:02.540
You, who befoul our beloved Earth!

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:05.290
No justice can come from loveless power!

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.540
Love is all!

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.050
Live for love! Die for love!

00:17:10.640 --> 00:17:13.220
We are the heirs to the throne of love!

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:14.640
Battle Lovers!

00:17:15.350 --> 00:17:16.450
Feel the power...

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:19.060
Of love!

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:21.930
Disorderly things!

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.610
Inadequate things! Superfluous things!

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:26.210
Destroy them all this instant!

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:27.160
Wait!

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:30.200
We're gonna defeat you!

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:30.870
What?

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:31.520
That's too abridged!

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.370
But we already introduced ourselves before!

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:37.010
I want to go home already, 
so let's get this done.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:39.010
That's a careless line no hero should say.

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:40.880
You're amazing, Yufuin-senpai.

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:40.880
What the heck?

00:17:40.880 --> 00:17:42.040
"Defeat you"?

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.500
How embarrassing.

00:17:44.260 --> 00:17:46.030
They're right to react like that.

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:48.120
Hey, do they recognize us?

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:50.130
Worry not!

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:54.180
Your images and voices have been altered 
to protect your personal information.

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:58.640
*Image and voices have been altered to protect privacy

00:17:54.670 --> 00:17:56.670
They'll still recognize us if we use our real names.

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.650
For now, I'm Cerulean!

00:17:58.650 --> 00:17:59.730
Take this!

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.060
Hey, that was dangerous!

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:08.030
Yu— Cerulean-senpai's really into it!

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.490
I told you, I want to get home.

00:18:10.490 --> 00:18:13.420
Five! An indivisible number!

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:15.570
Then I will erase you!

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:16.730
What was that?

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:20.750
The world must be beautifully 
symmetrical and even!

00:18:20.750 --> 00:18:22.990
What are you talking about?

00:18:25.130 --> 00:18:27.330
You mean, you don't like this kind of thing?

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.010
Are you stupid?!

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:33.130
Don't show me that thing!

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.140
Senpai!

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:46.100
What'd you do that for?!

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:51.020
I will destroy warped things 
and incomplete sets!

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.040
Why?

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:53.780
What's wrong with disposable chopsticks?

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.040
The splinters!

00:19:00.040 --> 00:19:03.790
The splinters from the 
chopsticks got Yu— got Scarlet!

00:19:03.790 --> 00:19:05.500
Those things really hurt.

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:19.880
This thing's making rattling noises!

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:23.780
A mass of chopsticks acts as my armor,

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:26.270
rendering your attacks useless!

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.020
The finish!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.440
If you hate disposable chopsticks that much,

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.620
don't use them to protect yourself!

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:41.870
Just bring your own chopsticks!

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:48.330
These irregular chopsticks you're trying to 
destroy have a great purpose behind them!

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:50.240
Purpose?!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:51.700
I'm talking about...

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:53.590
A child's rifle!

00:19:53.590 --> 00:19:56.350
Ch-Child's rifle?!

00:19:56.350 --> 00:19:59.300
Can something so cool exist 
in this world? No, it can't!

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.560
A rhetorical question?!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.970
Scarlet Lumiere!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.500
Sparkle, Lumiere of Love!

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:14.980
Flash, Purifying Aqua!

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.490
Pierce, Gallant Hurricane!

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:19.990
Roar, Raging Gaia!

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.490
Thrill, Blazing Ignit!

00:20:35.510 --> 00:20:38.790
Love Attack!

00:20:49.200 --> 00:20:52.360
Your inability to see disposable chopsticks
as anything but chopsticks was your downfall.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:55.360
Wash your used chopsticks and use them again!

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:59.960
Love Shower!

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.180
What is this sensation?

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:07.890
Comfort... Healing...

00:21:07.890 --> 00:21:10.740
So this is love...

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.210
Eco-friendly...

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:19.670
Love is over!

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.340
We told you, it's not!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:23.090
Well, whatever.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:27.050
One thing has become very clear.

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:30.320
They are our enemies.

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:32.810
<b>Kurotama Bath</b>

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:38.730
Yumoto. How's the bath?

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:40.900
Just perfect, Gora.

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:43.950
As I thought, there was no 
need for all five of us.

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:47.320
Yumoto just handled it all by himself. 
With the force of a storm.

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:48.860
I never got to show off.

00:21:48.860 --> 00:21:51.080
Try harder next time.

00:21:51.710 --> 00:21:53.920
That pisses me off! What's your 
problem, you overgrown rodent?

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:56.040
I am not a rodent!

00:21:56.040 --> 00:21:56.920
He's a marsupial.

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:58.550
What are you saying?!

00:21:59.780 --> 00:22:00.510
Huh?

00:22:00.510 --> 00:22:04.110
Will Mr. Tawaramura be okay 
in hot water like this?

00:22:04.110 --> 00:22:05.480
Ah, wait...

00:23:41.180 --> 00:23:43.280
A pretty boy contest at an all-boys' school?

00:23:43.280 --> 00:23:45.470
There's something wrong with this place.

00:23:45.470 --> 00:23:49.040
But the Ballet Club advisor, 
Kurotori, is really pushing for it.

00:23:49.040 --> 00:23:50.450
Ugh, what a pain.

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:54.900
Next Time

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:54.900
Feel Love, Narcissus!

00:23:50.680 --> 00:23:52.640
Next time: Feel Love, Narcissus!

00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:53.830
Love Making!
